    {
      "id": "quote:4870b19d7dbc9d45",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 369,
        "char_start": 232,
        "episode_id": "9833b47e-0cc8-50b9-a6da-65dc0f6d053f",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "Today's episode is sponsored by Adobe. Adobe Creative Cloud puts Lightroom, Photoshop, and Premiere on every device. Try adobe.com today.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 18000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 12000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p04_e02.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:4507f4eb8d409acf",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 466,
        "char_start": 369,
        "episode_id": "9833b47e-0cc8-50b9-a6da-65dc0f6d053f",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "Before we get into it \u2014 Ava Lemoyne was on last week talking about strobe positioning underwater.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 24000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 18000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p04_e02.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:54b81baea8f68434",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 635,
        "char_start": 545,
        "episode_id": "9833b47e-0cc8-50b9-a6da-65dc0f6d053f",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "I want to flag something \u2014 Ava Lemoyne mentioned this same dynamic a couple episodes back.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 36000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 30000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p04_e02.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:ff1189542e36ec13",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 742,
        "char_start": 635,
        "episode_id": "9833b47e-0cc8-50b9-a6da-65dc0f6d053f",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "What's the one heuristic you keep coming back to? What's the version of the question that actually matters?",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 42000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 36000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p04_e02.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:b86590c952552dbf",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 990,
        "char_start": 757,
        "episode_id": "9833b47e-0cc8-50b9-a6da-65dc0f6d053f",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-02",
        "text": "It comes down to this: Documentary frames carry the most weight when the photographer is closer than feels comfortable. We've seen this play out at teams using Capture One. I've watched this pattern hold across three different teams.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 48000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 42000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p04_e02.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    }
